[0.485, "o", "ROLE: You are a senior JavaScript engineer.\r\nTASK: Write a function that checks if a string is a valid Bangladeshi mobile number.\r\nCONTEXT: A valid number is 01, then one operator digit from 3 to 9, then 8 digits. The leading 0 may be replaced with the prefix +880 or 880.\r\nEXAMPLES:\r\n  \"+8801512345678\" -> true\r\n  \"0161234567\" -> false (too short)\r\nCONSTRAINTS:\r\n- Accept only these formats: 01XXXXXXXXX, 8801XXXXXXXXX, +8801XXXXXXXXX.\r\n- Reject any other input. Return a boolean. Never throw.\r\n- Use no library.\r\nOUTPUT FORMAT: Only one JavaScript function named isValidBDPhone(s). No other text.\r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "\r\n"]
